The deterministic grid auditor and its initial regression tests were adapted
from the user-provided pixel-art-qa-development-kit v0.2.0. Pixelwright adds
indexed logical-canvas generation, strict reusable profiles, batch inspection,
exact transparent-RGB policy, output preservation, provenance, complete cell
masks, packaging, documentation, and examples.

Pillow and NumPy are runtime dependencies installed separately. Their own
licenses apply to those packages; they are not bundled into Pixelwright ZIPs.

The sprite-gen atlas adapter follows the runtime manifest format published by
sprite-gen (https://github.com/aldegad/sprite-gen), licensed under Apache-2.0.
This is a data-format integration. Atlas validation does not install, import,
or execute sprite-gen, and sprite-gen code is not bundled into Pixelwright.
The tested contract baseline is sprite-gen 2.45.3, revision
59b2738a2e76ed7043d9691a230396ed6374a336. Machine-readable attribution and
compatibility details are in the skill's upstream-integrations.json.
